From c5699052a8f11698e948cf10d3bd290286d12357 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 05:03:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] M37 battle v3: a superweapon's force pulls out once the
 caps hold up its objectives

Measured in a grown computer town (Calhaven, the test city's resort, 1,799 residents):
the robot knocked down five of its six military objectives by step 174, then stood at
the sixth until the clock ran out (1,585 steps): the sixth can't fall, because the
superweapon caps allow five wrecked city buildings and every military objective is one.
A longer step limit would only have kept it standing there longer.

Now a battle that brought a superweapon withdraws as soon as every objective still
standing is one the caps won't let fall (Battle.capsHold, checked with the others in
check(); no draws). There the robot is done in 307 steps, with the same five wrecked
and one collapsed. Battles without a superweapon are untouched (they still wait for the
clock), and a test shows both.

scripts/dev/superstrike.ts: each superweapon against a computer neighbour's grown town.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PaNjihW6RqXZz8HFLo1j3d
