From f9cf234b8c1ef6db8915c5f51ea980bb8c1eaca7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 05:15:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] M37 battle v3: the sky fortress carries bomb drones

The fortress launched its 16 drones and did nothing: a drone hits a building for
attack 5 x siege 0.2 = 1. Now `carries.siege` (15 on the fortress) is the siege of
what a carrier brings, applied to the carried units only, and those bomb drones dive
on the force's objectives first, then the guns (other units still take on guns first).
Their bombs are heavy shots (siege >= 1), so interceptors can stop them and misses
stray and crater, as other bombs do. Drones trained and sent as drones are unchanged.

Calibrated over nine grown computer resorts (seeds citybloom, alpha ... hotel), siege
0.2 / 10 / 15 / 20 (objectives down of 54; wrecked of the cap's 45):
- as grown: 1 / 39 / 45 / 45 objectives (the robot: 45), every town at the cap of
  five wrecked from 15 up;
- every gun post manned (defences 40): 10 / 25 / 38 at 10 / 15 / 20, two towns shooting
  all sixteen down at 15.
15 matches the robot where the town is as grown and still lets anti-air win.

Tests: the fortress's bomb drones in the grown resort (as many objectives down and
wrecks as the robot, drones shot down, all sixteen and less damage with every post
manned); bomb drones carried, a fortress's escort drones and a plain drone raid at 0.2;
four battles without a superweapon pinned to hashes taken on a037629. The launch test's
town now has sturdy military buildings, so the force stays to launch all sixteen (its
own depot and bunker fall to the first five bomb drones).

