From 53318a3a509a40002803613d2d3de3cd54e6ede6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 05:26:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] M37 battle v3: the clockwork whale's torpedo pods reach a
 computer town's seafront

The whale surfaced off the coast and never fired. Measured in nine grown computer
resorts (seeds citybloom, alpha ... hotel, at the test size): its military stands
745-1,138 m from the water nearest it, and the nearest building of any kind 482-844 m
from where the whale lies (still 511-540 m at 7,500-9,300 residents). With its 450 m
range nothing in any of them is ever in reach, so firing at "the nearest structures in
reach" alone would still do nothing.

Now the whale, surfaced, chooses its own target (chooseFromSea; no dice, nearest first,
ties to the lower index): within its 450 m guns, units (those that can hit back first)
and manned guns that can fire on it; beyond, its torpedo pods reach buildings within
`dives.reach` (1,000 m): the force's objectives first, then whatever stands nearest. A
gun that can fire on it is never a pod target, so a coastal gun (480 m) beyond its
450 m still outranges it, as the design means; a bunker that can't answer it is podded
like any building. Pods are heavy shots: interceptors can stop them, misses stray.

Reach 800 / 900 / 1,000 / 1,200 m over the nine towns: 106 / 189 / 213 / 213 collapsed,
4 / 7 / 11 / 12 wrecked; at 1,000 every town loses 23-24 buildings (the superweapon
collapse cap), 0-2 objectives; full-size towns 9-25 (the wreck cap ends two of them
early). Its other numbers are the design's (attack 220, siege 3, reload 8, 600 steps up).

Tests: in the grown resort the whale surfaces where nothing stands within 450 m, fires
pods and knocks at least ten buildings down within the caps, then dives and goes home;
handmade: a coastal gun 470 m off hits it and is left alone while its pods take the
bunker and depot from beyond 450 m, and the same gun 400 m off falls. The older whale
test's coastal gun is built to take a few pods (5,000 hp), so the two still trade shots
(the whale now opens fire from further out, which changes the dice, and its first pod
at the gun hit).

