From ccb89838da913d806dd8b108b7054fe47bb763ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 05:37:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Battles: target searches walk the grid's cells without
 sorting them; battlebench --dump

Choosing a target (choose, the whale's chooseFromSea) and finding cover take the best by
a total order (rank, distance, index) or return the same value whatever they find
first, so the structures near a unit needn't be copied and sorted for them:
structsNear fills a reused list in no set order. Stamping, strays and craters, whose
answer hangs on the order, keep the sorted nearStructs. Every result is unchanged
(the pinned hashes, the version 2 replays, the M36 goldens, and the superweapon
strikes in nine grown towns battle for battle).

The whale's raid on the 100k bench city, fought at once (input from battlebench
--dump): 117 / 81 / 48 / 49 ms over four runs in one process before, 67 / 62 / 24 /
22 ms after; that battle's tick average cold 0.87 -> 0.48 ms (the machine shared with
another session's test run, so within about 20 %).

scripts/dev/battlebench.ts --dump file: writes the whole-battle input as JSON.

