From 3bdc062e4bb3d383ebfd7ecddf2abf9d05dbaa6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 06:14:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Battles: the robot keeps to the road over water, and
 walks (never jumps) to its next objective

Two defects found in review of the robot's moves (both only in a battle with the robot):

- It left the road as soon as it was within 500 m of its objective in a straight line, whatever
  lay between; walk() takes water ahead as arrival, so with a bridged river in the way it stood
  at the bank (Hold) for good. On lineLayout with a river at x 576-672 the road bridges, a tank
  raided the depot and the robot destroyed nothing. Now it leaves the road only when the line to
  its objective is dry (dryLine, sampled every 2 m as finely as it walks), and otherwise drives on
  by road. Should water stop its walk all the same, it walks back to the nearest road and reaches
  that objective by road (`wet`).
- On a new objective, retarget() put it back on the road at the point it had left, up to 500 m
  behind: one tick moved it 446 m. Now it walks straight to the new objective when that's within
  500 m over dry ground, else to the nearest road point it can walk to on a road that leads there
  (nearestRoad, rejoinRoad), turning the right way along it (face); pulling out, it likewise walks
  to the nearest road that leads out.

No draws added. Battles without the robot are unchanged (the pinned hashes, version 2 replays and
M36 goldens pass); in nine grown towns the robot's strikes are as before, a few steps longer.
Tests reproduce both (they failed before: objectives 0/2; a 446 m jump), and the grown-town
hook gets 60 s for a busy machine.

